[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. Read the reports, not
their subject lines, and it holds three problems. The queued parser fix closes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. Two of its problems need fixes of their own.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** A tenant whose locale writes the
day first gets day and month swapped: "Booked for 2 July. The invite says 7 February." This is
the bug #4471 names, and the queued fix is for it. Every tenant on file is day first.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`. People at a day-first tenant on booking-v3 type what the hint says, and the form
reads it the tenant's way, day first. Same swap, different bug: the parser fix does not touch
the form's hint. Only reports sent through the form, at a booking-v3 tenant, are this.

**`day-shift`: the date moves by one day.** These dates are not swapped. "Tuesday 6 October
showed as Monday." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting."
An invite that "arrived before I made the booking". The day depends on where the reader is:
a time zone bug, not a format bug. [The cause table](/kb/incidents/4471) counts these under
`parser` and footnotes them; the parser fix will not fix them.

## How three became one

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the **subject line** and
  nobody reads the body. Every report here has a subject that says "wrong day" in some form, so
  all three problems went into one ticket. The decision planned for one bug under different
  words; it did not plan for different bugs under the same words.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant and the
  way in (`causes.ts`). The two disagree, so the tag cannot split the ticket.
- The export repeats reports across its pages. Count by id.

## What the desk does now

- Keep #4471 for `parser` only. Move `hint` and `day-shift` reports to the tickets above.
- When a report says "one day off", read it before you merge it: that is `day-shift`.
- Re-read [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe): it was last reviewed in 2024.

